WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.235
With me now, Homeland Security Secretary

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.703
Alejandro Mayorkas.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.071
Thank you so much for joining me

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:05.672
this morning.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.507
You are getting regular updates

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:08.975
from the southern border.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:10.710
What is the latest

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.645
with regard to border crossings?

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.048
And do you believe the surge has peaked

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.118
again over the past two days?

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.452
The United States border

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.121
patrol has experienced

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:24.491
a 50% drop in the number of encounters

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.726
versus what we were experiencing

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:28.395
earlier in the week

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:31.464
before Title 42 ended at midnight

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:32.832
on Thursday.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.167
It is still early.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.902
We are in day three.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:36.336
But, you know,

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.737
we've been planning

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.206
for this transition for months and months

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.709
and we've been executing on our plan

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.511
and we will continue to do so.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.780
So it's too early to say whether

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.182
the surge has peaked. It is.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.283
It is too early.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.785
But the numbers that we have experienced

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:54.721
over the past two days are markedly down

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.756
over what they were prior

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.158
to the end of Title 42.

00:00:58.158 --> 00:01:00.126
What are the numbers? 5000.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.428
So we have seen

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:04.197
I think approximately 6300

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:08.668
on Friday and about 4200 yesterday

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.971
by the United States Border Patrol,

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.007
and we saw over 10,000

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.842
before the end of Title 42

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.677
earlier last week.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.212
Why do you think that is?

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:22.115
Because we have communicated very clearly

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.517
a vitally important message

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.319
to the individuals who are thinking

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.254
of arriving at our southern border.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.023
There is a lawful,

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.392
safe and orderly way to arrive

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.960
in the United States.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.795
That is through the pathways

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.263
that President Biden

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.966
has expanded in an unprecedented way.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.235
And then there's a consequence

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.470
if one does not use

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.004
those lawful pathways.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.540
And that consequence is removal

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.243
from the United States, a deportation,

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.446
and encountering a five year ban

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.248
on reentry and possible

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.449
criminal prosecution.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.951
You say that you

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:00.153
at the Department of Homeland Security,

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.187
you have been preparing.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.789
Not everybody agrees with you,

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.424
as I know you are aware,

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:05.492
not just Republicans,

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.993
even some Democrats,

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:07.861
even those

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:10.263
who represent parts of the border.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.665
Arizona Congressman Ruben Gallego

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:13.166
said, quote,

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.301
Federal agencies have had time to plan,

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.604
but their efforts have fallen short.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.172
How do you respond to

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:21.241
him and some other Democrats

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.109
who say that you've fallen short?

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.245
I would respectfully disagree.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.080
We have been planning for months

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.948
and months over a year and a half.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.017
We have surged resources,

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.921
asylum officers, border patrol

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.589
agents, processing

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.758
coordinators to do the data entry work.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:39.959
So our Border Patrol

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.061
agents can be out in the field.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.631
We've expanded our holding capacity

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.266
in Border Patrol stations.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.667
We've added beds

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.702
to Immigration and Customs Enforcement

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.638
in our detention facilities.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.673
We've increased our transportation

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:56.009
resources, the number of flights,

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.111
the removal of flights

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.846
with our foreign partners.

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.915
We're setting up regional processing

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.082
centers now.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.184
It's extraordinary.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.819
We've done over the past 18 months or so.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.955
There's a debate in your party

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.690
about how restrictive

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.959
the United States should be towards

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.661
asylum claims.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.496
What's your philosophy on that?

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.598
So as the asylum system

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:19.933
has been

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:20.633
and continues

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.869
to be a jewel of the United States,

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:25.505
we take great, great pride as a country

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:26.372
in this world

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.308
to provide humanitarian relief

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:30.310
for those who qualify.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.812
But the landscape of migration

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.814
has changed dramatically over the past

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.216
ten plus years.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.917
No longer are individuals

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.086
arriving at our border

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.721
of their own volition.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:44.357
They are arriving in the hands

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:48.127
of smugglers that wreak such tragedy,

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:50.597
such trauma upon their lives.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.565
The the cartels,

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.400
the smuggling organizations

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.935
control the land.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.437
And so we have

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:59.639
not only a security imperative,

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.342
but a humanitarian responsibility

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:04.377
to cut those smugglers out.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:04.777
And that's

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.512
precisely what we as

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.648
an administrator, has done.

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.083
We have attacked

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.818
the smuggling organizations

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:13.653
with our law enforcement authorities.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:17.523
We've arrested more than 10,000 smugglers

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:19.392
President Biden

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:19.926
has led

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.361
the greatest expansion

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:21.995
of lawful

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.763
pathways ever

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:26.432
through family reunification programs,

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:27.734
through expedited

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.302
refugee processing,

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.471
through the regional processing centers

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.605
that we're now building.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:33.740
But we have an obligation

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.576
to deliver consequences at our border

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.678
to not only manage our border,

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.546
but to cut the smugglers out.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:41.147
You are

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.949
well aware the House of Representatives

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.250
passed a sweeping

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.752
border security bill this week.

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:46.819
I know there's a lot in there

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.221
that you do not like,

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:49.889
but there is funding

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.424
for more border agents,

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.525
which I know that you said

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:53.726
that you very much need

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.561
more technology at the border.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.897
Have you spoken with House Speaker

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:59.565
McCarthy directly

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.567
about the possibility

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.436
of finding compromise here?

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.871
I have not.

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:07.273
We have been calling on Congress

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:08.875
to pass legislation

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:11.444
to fix what everyone agrees is a broken

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.645
immigration system.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.147
We've been asking for that

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:16.082
for more than two decades.

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:16.683
On day

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:19.719
one of his presidency, President Biden

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:22.522
presented a legislative package.

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:23.623
The proposal

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:25.658
right now, what we are asking for

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:27.527
and we are really

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:29.762
we in need of desperately as a country

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:32.865
is immigration reform to fix the system,

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.534
not to dismantle it,

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:35.735
which is what this proposal

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:36.836
really provides.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:37.603
That's been stuck

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:39.639
inside partizan gridlock for

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.407
15 years or so. I

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:43.776
want to ask about

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.912
something my next guest is going to say

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.313
this is Republican Congressman

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:47.880
Mark Green.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.382
He's the chairman of the Homeland

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:51.484
Security Committee.

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:54.187
He has indicated he wants to impeach you

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.321
for the way

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.256
that you've handled the border crisis.

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.558
Are you worried

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:00.526
that that process is going to start

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:02.995
and how will you react?

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:06.666
Dana, I am focused on the work

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.568
in front of us.

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:10.002
Meeting the challenge

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:11.204
not only with respect

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:12.572
to the southern border,

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:15.108
but meeting the challenge of cyber

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:18.244
the cyber threat from cyber criminals

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.880
and adverse foreign nations as states.

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:24.083
I am focused on the increasing

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:25.752
severity and frequency

00:06:25.752 --> 00:06:27.487
of extreme weather events.

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:30.490
I am focused on the adverse actions

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:32.825
of the People's Republic of China,

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:35.595
North Korea, Iran, Russia.

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:38.030
I am focused on the work

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.932
of the Department of Homeland Security.

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:42.602
I will continue to focus on that work

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.270
throughout my tenure.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.738
Homeland Security Secretary

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:46.773
Alejandro Mayorkas,

00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:47.540
thank you so much

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:48.541
for joining me this morning.

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:49.108
Thank you, Dana.

